    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Represents an interpretation of a binary container.</para><para>An interpretation is a collection of the parts of a binary specimen that represent a coherent program, library, core dump, etc. For instance, a Windows PE executable has a DOS interpretation and a Windows interpretation<ndash/>really two executables in the one container. All the DOS-related stuff will be under one <ref refid="classSgAsmInterpretation" kindref="compound">SgAsmInterpretation</ref> AST and all the Windows-related stuff will be under another <ref refid="classSgAsmInterpretation" kindref="compound">SgAsmInterpretation</ref> AST. </para>    </detaileddescription>
